# Releases published BEFORE the promotion gate existed, one `tag  reason` per
# line. The audit in .github/scripts/audit_release_wiring.sh refuses any FINAL
# release whose tag was cut from a tree that does not carry the pre-upload gate
# step; a tag cut before the step was written cannot carry it, and reporting
# that as a defect forever would make the audit noise rather than a signal.
#
# This file is an ESCAPE HATCH and every entry is printed loudly on every run.
# Adding a line here for a NEW release defeats the audit, which is the one thing
# the audit exists to prevent - it is not a way to make a red go away, and the
# audit CHECKS the claim: an entry whose release was published after the gate
# step entered Release.yml is refused anyway, exemption or not.
v0.1.0  published 2026-08, long before any promotion gate existed in this repo
